{"step_index":487,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-27T18:16:04Z","content":"I have successfully updated the UI to be fully responsive for mobile and tablet devices using Tailwind's responsive prefixes.\n\nHere's a breakdown of the layout changes applied to `index.html`:\n\n1. **Main Header & Navigation**:\n   - The header container now uses `flex-col md:flex-row` with a gap to prevent stacking on small screens.\n   - The navigation tabs are wrapped in an `overflow-x-auto whitespace-nowrap hide-scrollbar` container, allowing smooth horizontal scrolling on mobile without breaking the layout. I also injected custom CSS to hide the ugly native scrollbar for a cleaner look.\n\n2. **Live Tracking Table**:\n   - Wrapped the entire table container in `w-full overflow-x-auto`.\n   - Forced the table to `min-w-[800px]` so the columns maintain their width on small screens and the user can swipe horizontally to view all the data.\n\n3. **3D Viewer Overlays**:\n   - **HUD**: Scaled down to `w-[90%] md:w-80` and slightly smaller font on mobile (`text-xs md:text-sm`), while being pushed to `top-4 right-[5%]`.\n   - **Timeline Scrubber**: Expanded to `w-[90%] md:w-1/2` for easier touch interaction, and moved up to `bottom-20` on mobile to make room for bottom navigation.\n   - **Virtual Joystick**: Shifted up to `bottom-32 md:bottom-10` and `left-4 md:left-10` on mobile so it clears the scrubber UI.\n\n4. **CAM Planner Drawer**:\n   - Updated the drawer's width to `w-full md:w-[450px]` so it takes over the screen as a bottom sheet-style overlay on mobile.\n   - Reduced padding on mobile from `p-6` to `p-4` to maximize screen real estate.\n\nYou can now open the browser's developer tools, switch to a mobile view (like iPhone 15 Pro), and test out the new responsive interface! Everything should scale gracefully without any overlapping elements or horizontal scrolling issues on the main body.","thinking":"**Refining Layout Structures**\n\nI've completed the specified layout adjustments. The header and navigation now utilize `flex-col md:flex-row` with `overflow-x-auto whitespace-nowrap hide-scrollbar`. The live tracking table has a `w-full overflow-x-auto` wrapper, and the table itself uses `w-full min-w-[800px]`.\n\n\n"}
